The vulnerability occurs when processing an SCTP INIT chunk with numerous invalid parameters. For each parameter, the kernel adds error data to a reply chunk, repeatedly calling `sctp_addto_chunk`. This can cause the 16-bit chunk length field to wrap around, leading to memory corruption and a kernel panic.

The patch prevents this by explicitly checking for an integer overflow before updating the chunk length and allocating memory.

