The key changes are:
1.  The local variable `chunklen` is changed from `int` to `__u16` to match the type of the length field in the SCTP header.
2.  A new `__u16` variable, `newlen`, is introduced to store the calculated new length of the chunk.
3.  An overflow check, `if (newlen < chunklen)`, is added. This detects if adding the new data length caused the 16-bit unsigned integer to wrap around.
