Patch code.response:
The patch for CVE-2020-12464 addresses a use-after-free vulnerability in the `usb_sg_cancel` function by taking a reference to the USB device before canceling the URBs (USB Request Blocks) and releasing it afterward. This ensures the device structure is not deallocated prematurely.

The patched code is as follows:

```c
void usb_sg_cancel(struct usb_sg_request *io)
{
	unsigned long flags;
	struct usb_device *dev = io->dev;
	int i, retval;

	spin_lock_irqsave(&io->lock, flags);
	if (io->status) {
		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&io->lock, flags);
		return;
	}

	usb_get_dev(dev);

	/* shut everything down */
	io->status = -ECONNRESET;
	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&io->lock, flags);

	for (i = io->entries - 1; i >= 0; --i) {
		usb_block_urb(io->urbs[i]);

		retval = usb_unlink_urb(io->urbs[i]);
		if (retval != -EINPROGRESS
		    && retval != -ENODEV
		    && retval != -EBUSY
		    && retval != -EIDRM)
			dev_warn(&io->dev->dev, "%s, unlink --> %d\n",
				 __func__, retval);
	}

	usb_put_dev(dev);
}
```

