When the cleanup logic calls `kvm_free_lapic`, it unconditionally attempts to call `kvm_iodevice_destroy(&apic->dev)`, operating on uninitialized data. This leads to a kernel crash and a denial of service.

The patch fixes this by adding a conditional check in `kvm_free_lapic` to ensure `apic->dev` has been initialized (by checking if `apic->dev.ops` is non-NULL) before attempting to destroy it.

