The patch introduces a simple but effective bounds check. It defines a maximum permissible allocation size (`MAX_STACK_ALLOC`) and rejects any request where `len` exceeds this limit, preventing the underflow.

Here is a representative code diff for the `x86` architecture (`arch/x86/include/asm/compat.h`):

