The patch introduces a check to validate the requested allocation length against the current stack pointer before performing the subtraction. If the requested length is greater than the stack pointer, the function returns `NULL` instead of a corrupted pointer.

The code changes for the x86 architecture (`arch/x86/include/asm/compat.h`) are as follows:

