A proof-of-concept exploit for CVE-2010-1636 is publicly available. The exploit demonstrates how a local user can read data from a file for which they only have write permissions. It works by opening a source file with the `O_WRONLY` flag and then using the `BTRFS_IOC_CLONE` ioctl to copy its contents to a new destination file, which the user can then read freely.

