The exploit works by creating a CAN BCM socket and setting up an RX filter. It then uses two threads: one thread continuously closes and re-opens the socket file descriptor to trigger `bcm_release`, while the other thread sends CAN frames to the same socket, triggering the `bcm_rx_handler`. This race can cause the handler to access memory that has already been freed by `bcm_release`, resulting in a kernel panic or crash.

