The patch for CVE-2021-23133 fixes a race condition by ensuring proper locking when a Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP) socket is destroyed. The vulnerability occurs because the `sctp_destroy_sock` function removes an element from the `auto_asconf_splist` list without acquiring the `addr_wq_lock`. Meanwhile, the `sctp_init_sock` function uses this lock when adding to the same list.

